{"nbformat":4,"nbformat_minor":5,"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"display_name":"Python 3","language":"python","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.10"}},"cells":[{"id":"0443e6e4","cell_type":"markdown","source":"# MNIST MLP3: every-step maximum one-sided TraceLogRG test\n\nThis second notebook tests whether the original null result was caused by the 25-step cadence or the 10% correction cap.\n\nIt uses the strongest faithful version of the **existing** implementation:\n\n- inspect the completed AdamW displacement on every minibatch (`rg_apply_every_steps=1`);\n- use the full one-sided projection (`rg_correction_scale=1.0`);\n- remove the norm cap (`rg_max_correction_ratio=None`);\n- keep the WeightWatcher-normalized trace-log geometry;\n- do **not** control $\\alpha$, $\\beta_E$, ERG gap, or correlation traps.\n\nWeightWatcher is measured at initialization and after each epoch; the optimizer check itself runs every step. The default is 8 epochs because FC1 crossed below $\\alpha=2$ by about epoch 4 in the original run. Change `epochs=20` for the full horizon.","metadata":{}},{"id":"5f9a6d69","cell_type":"code","metadata":{},"execution_count":null,"source":"from pathlib import Path\nimport math, subprocess, sys\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nimport torch\nimport weightwatcher as ww\nfrom IPython.display import display\n\nPACKAGE_ROOT = None\nfor candidate in [Path.cwd(), *Path.cwd().parents]:\n    direct = candidate / \"rg_trace_log\"\n    nested = candidate / \"optimizers\" / \"trace_log_tracker\" / \"rg_trace_log\"\n    if direct.is_dir():\n        PACKAGE_ROOT = candidate\n        break\n    if nested.is_dir():\n        PACKAGE_ROOT = candidate / \"optimizers\" / \"trace_log_tracker\"\n        break\nif PACKAGE_ROOT is None:\n    raise RuntimeError(\"Open this notebook from a clone of rg_optimizers.\")\n\nINSTALL_DEPENDENCIES = False\nif INSTALL_DEPENDENCIES:\n    subprocess.check_call([\n        sys.executable, \"-m\", \"pip\", \"install\", \"-q\", \"-r\",\n        str(PACKAGE_ROOT / \"requirements.txt\"),\n    ])\nif str(PACKAGE_ROOT) not in sys.path:\n    sys.path.insert(0, str(PACKAGE_ROOT))\n\nfrom rg_trace_log import MNISTExperimentConfig, run_mnist_comparison\n\nCOLORS = {\n    \"AdamW baseline\": \"#0072B2\",       # blue in every comparison plot\n    \"AdamW + TraceLogRG\": \"#009E73\",   # green in every comparison plot\n}\nGREEN = {\"dark\": \"#006D2C\", \"mid\": \"#31A354\", \"light\": \"#A1D99B\"}\n\nconfig = MNISTExperimentConfig(\n    seed=1337,\n    epochs=8,                 # set to 20 for the full previous horizon\n    batch_size=128,\n    learning_rate=1e-3,\n    weight_decay=1e-2,\n    grad_clip_norm=1.0,\n    rg_mode=\"one_sided\",\n    rg_normalization=\"weightwatcher\",\n    rg_gamma=0.10,\n    rg_ridge_relative=1e-6,\n    rg_min_retained=5,\n    rg_correction_scale=1.0,\n    rg_max_correction_ratio=None,\n    rg_apply_every_steps=1,\n    rg_warmup_steps=0,\n    ww_min_evals=10,\n    ww_max_evals=None,\n    n_log_shells=5,\n    min_retained_for_beta=20,\n    min_decades_for_beta=0.50,\n)\nassert config.rg_mode == \"one_sided\"\nassert config.rg_apply_every_steps == 1\nassert config.rg_correction_scale == 1.0\nassert config.rg_max_correction_ratio is None\nassert config.rg_warmup_steps == 0\n\nprint(\"Package root:\", PACKAGE_ROOT)\nprint(\"Torch:\", torch.__version__)\nprint(\"WeightWatcher:\", getattr(ww, \"__version__\", \"unknown\"))\nprint(\"Maximum intervention:\", config)","outputs":[]},{"id":"5a27a51f","cell_type":"code","metadata":{},"execution_count":null,"source":"result = run_mnist_comparison(\n    config,\n    data_dir=PACKAGE_ROOT / \"data\",\n    progress=True,\n)\nOUTPUT_DIR = PACKAGE_ROOT / \"results_every_step_max_intervention\"\nresult.save(OUTPUT_DIR)\nprint(\"Results saved to:\", OUTPUT_DIR.resolve())","outputs":[]},{"id":"bf95385b","cell_type":"code","metadata":{},"execution_count":null,"source":"def ordered_runs(frame):\n    return [\n        run for run in (\"AdamW baseline\", \"AdamW + TraceLogRG\")\n        if run in set(frame[\"run\"].dropna().astype(str))\n    ]\n\ndef fc1_rows(history, min_epoch=1):\n    rows = history.loc[\n        history[\"layer_name\"].astype(str).str.endswith(\"fc1\")\n        & history[\"status\"].eq(\"ok\")\n        & history[\"epoch\"].ge(min_epoch)\n    ].copy()\n    return rows.sort_values([\"run\", \"epoch\"])\n\ndef plot_run_metric(frame, x, y, title, ylabel, reference=None):\n    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(9, 5), dpi=140)\n    for run in ordered_runs(frame):\n        group = frame.loc[frame[\"run\"].eq(run)].sort_values(x)\n        ax.plot(\n            group[x], group[y], marker=\"o\", markersize=5.5, linewidth=2.4,\n            color=COLORS[run], label=run,\n        )\n    if reference is not None:\n        ax.axhline(\n            reference, linestyle=\"--\", linewidth=1.5, color=\"black\",\n            alpha=0.7, label=f\"reference = {reference:g}\",\n        )\n    ax.set_xlabel(\"Epoch\")\n    ax.set_ylabel(ylabel)\n    ax.set_title(title)\n    ax.grid(alpha=0.25)\n    ax.legend()\n    plt.tight_layout()\n    plt.show()\n\nfc1 = fc1_rows(result.weightwatcher)\nplot_run_metric(\n    fc1, \"epoch\", \"alpha\",\n    r\"FC1: fitted WeightWatcher $\\alpha$\",\n    r\"WeightWatcher $\\alpha$\", reference=2.0,\n)\n\nalpha_wide = fc1.pivot(index=\"epoch\", columns=\"run\", values=\"alpha\").sort_index()\nalpha_wide[\"TraceLogRG minus baseline\"] = (\n    alpha_wide[\"AdamW + TraceLogRG\"] - alpha_wide[\"AdamW baseline\"]\n)\ndisplay(alpha_wide)\n\nfig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(9, 4.5), dpi=140)\nax.plot(\n    alpha_wide.index, alpha_wide[\"TraceLogRG minus baseline\"],\n    marker=\"o\", linewidth=2.4, color=COLORS[\"AdamW + TraceLogRG\"],\n)\nax.axhline(0.0, linestyle=\"--\", linewidth=1.5, color=\"black\", alpha=0.7)\nax.set_xlabel(\"Epoch\")\nax.set_ylabel(r\"$\\alpha_{\\rm TraceLogRG}-\\alpha_{\\rm AdamW}$\")\nax.set_title(r\"FC1: fitted $\\alpha$ difference\")\nax.grid(alpha=0.25)\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()\n\nplot_run_metric(\n    result.performance, \"epoch\", \"train_acc\",\n    \"Train accuracy\", \"Train accuracy\",\n)\nplot_run_metric(\n    result.performance, \"epoch\", \"test_acc\",\n    \"Test accuracy\", \"Test accuracy\",\n)\nplot_run_metric(\n    fc1, \"epoch\", \"trace_log_midpoint_per_eval\",\n    \"FC1: midpoint trace-log coordinate\",\n    \"Trace-log per retained eigenvalue\", reference=0.0,\n)","outputs":[]},{"id":"af8d093b","cell_type":"code","metadata":{},"execution_count":null,"source":"# Verify that the FC1 check ran every minibatch and determine whether it fired.\nif result.rg_steps.empty:\n    raise RuntimeError(\"No step-level RG diagnostics were recorded.\")\n\nsteps = result.rg_steps.loc[\n    result.rg_steps[\"parameter\"].astype(str).str.endswith(\"fc1.weight\")\n].copy()\nif steps.empty:\n    raise RuntimeError(\"No FC1 step diagnostics were found.\")\n\nsteps[\"fired\"] = steps[\"status\"].eq(\"ok\")\nsteps[\"negative_base_drift\"] = steps[\"base_trace_log_drift\"].lt(0.0)\nsteps[\"abs_base_drift\"] = steps[\"base_trace_log_drift\"].abs()\nsteps[\"abs_corrected_drift\"] = steps[\"corrected_trace_log_drift\"].abs()\nsteps[\"corrected_when_fired\"] = steps[\"abs_corrected_drift\"].where(steps[\"fired\"])\n\nexpected_per_epoch = math.ceil(60_000 / config.batch_size)\nby_epoch = steps.groupby(\"epoch\").agg(\n    expected_steps=(\"global_step\", lambda x: expected_per_epoch),\n    unique_steps=(\"global_step\", \"nunique\"),\n    opportunities=(\"global_step\", \"size\"),\n    fired_count=(\"fired\", \"sum\"),\n    fired_fraction=(\"fired\", \"mean\"),\n    negative_drift_fraction=(\"negative_base_drift\", \"mean\"),\n    geometry_failures=(\"status\", lambda x: x.eq(\"geometry_failed\").sum()),\n    mean_correction_ratio=(\"correction_ratio\", \"mean\"),\n    median_correction_ratio=(\"correction_ratio\", \"median\"),\n    max_correction_ratio=(\"correction_ratio\", \"max\"),\n    cap_fraction=(\n        \"correction_capped\",\n        lambda x: x.fillna(False).astype(bool).mean(),\n    ),\n    mean_abs_base_drift=(\"abs_base_drift\", \"mean\"),\n    mean_abs_corrected_drift=(\"abs_corrected_drift\", \"mean\"),\n    max_abs_corrected_when_fired=(\"corrected_when_fired\", \"max\"),\n)\nby_epoch[\"coverage_fraction\"] = by_epoch[\"unique_steps\"] / expected_per_epoch\ndisplay(by_epoch)\n\nfired = steps.loc[steps[\"fired"]].copy()\ncoverage = steps[\"global_step\"].nunique() / (expected_per_epoch * config.epochs)\nif fired.empty:\n    max_corrected = np.nan\n    residual_fraction = np.nan\nelse:\n    max_corrected = fired[\"corrected_trace_log_drift\"].abs().max()\n    denominator = fired[\"base_trace_log_drift\"].abs().sum()\n    residual_fraction = (\n        fired[\"corrected_trace_log_drift\"].abs().sum() / denominator\n        if denominator > 0 else np.nan\n    )\n\nsummary = pd.Series({\n    \"expected FC1 opportunities\": expected_per_epoch * config.epochs,\n    \"recorded FC1 opportunities\": len(steps),\n    \"coverage fraction\": coverage,\n    \"fraction with negative base drift\": steps[\"negative_base_drift\"].mean(),\n    \"fraction actually corrected\": steps[\"fired\"].mean(),\n    \"geometry failures\": steps[\"status\"].eq(\"geometry_failed\").sum(),\n    \"mean correction / AdamW step\": fired[\"correction_ratio\"].mean(),\n    \"median correction / AdamW step\": fired[\"correction_ratio\"].median(),\n    \"maximum correction / AdamW step\": fired[\"correction_ratio\"].max(),\n    \"fraction hitting cap\": steps[\"correction_capped\"].fillna(False).astype(bool).mean(),\n    \"maximum |corrected drift| when fired\": max_corrected,\n    \"sum |corrected drift| / sum |base drift| when fired\": residual_fraction,\n}, name=\"FC1 every-step one-sided projection\")\ndisplay(summary.to_frame())\n\nfig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(9, 4.5), dpi=140)\nax.plot(\n    by_epoch.index, by_epoch[\"negative_drift_fraction\"], marker=\"o\",\n    linewidth=2.2, color=GREEN[\"dark\"], label=\"negative base-drift fraction\",\n)\nax.plot(\n    by_epoch.index, by_epoch[\"fired_fraction\"], marker=\"o\",\n    linewidth=2.2, color=GREEN[\"light\"], label=\"actual correction fraction\",\n)\nax.set_ylim(-0.02, 1.02)\nax.set_xlabel(\"Epoch\")\nax.set_ylabel(\"Fraction of FC1 steps\")\nax.set_title(\"FC1: did the one-sided correction fire?\")\nax.grid(alpha=0.25)\nax.legend()\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()\n\nif not fired.empty:\n    fired = fired.sort_values(\"global_step\")\n    fired[\"rolling_median\"] = fired[\"correction_ratio\"].rolling(100, min_periods=1).median()\n\n    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10, 4.5), dpi=140)\n    ax.scatter(\n        fired[\"global_step\"], fired[\"correction_ratio\"], s=9, alpha=0.20,\n        color=GREEN[\"mid\"], label=\"individual correction\",\n    )\n    ax.plot(\n        fired[\"global_step\"], fired[\"rolling_median\"], linewidth=2.2,\n        color=GREEN[\"dark\"], label=\"100-correction rolling median\",\n    )\n    ax.set_xlabel(\"Optimizer step\")\n    ax.set_ylabel(r\"$\\|\\Delta W_{\\rm correction}\\|/\\|\\Delta W_{\\rm AdamW}\\|$\")\n    ax.set_title(\"FC1: uncapped correction magnitude\")\n    ax.grid(alpha=0.25)\n    ax.legend()\n    plt.tight_layout()\n    plt.show()\n\n    drift = fired.groupby(\"epoch\").agg(\n        selected_base_drift=(\"base_trace_log_drift\", \"sum\"),\n        drift_after_projection=(\"corrected_trace_log_drift\", \"sum\"),\n    )\n    display(drift)\n\n    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(9, 4.5), dpi=140)\n    ax.plot(\n        drift.index, drift[\"selected_base_drift\"], marker=\"o\",\n        linewidth=2.2, color=GREEN[\"dark\"], label=\"selected base drift\",\n    )\n    ax.plot(\n        drift.index, drift[\"drift_after_projection\"], marker=\"o\",\n        linewidth=2.2, color=GREEN[\"light\"], label=\"drift after projection\",\n    )\n    ax.axhline(0.0, linestyle=\"--\", linewidth=1.4, color=\"black\", alpha=0.7)\n    ax.set_xlabel(\"Epoch\")\n    ax.set_ylabel(\"Summed first-order trace-log drift\")\n    ax.set_title(\"FC1: selected drift before and after correction\")\n    ax.grid(alpha=0.25)\n    ax.legend()\n    plt.tight_layout()\n    plt.show()\n\nsteps.to_csv(OUTPUT_DIR / \"fc1_every_step_diagnostics.csv\", index=False)\nby_epoch.to_csv(OUTPUT_DIR / \"fc1_every_step_summary_by_epoch.csv\")","outputs":[]},{"id":"1efe2c35","cell_type":"code","metadata":{},"execution_count":null,"source":"# Automatic diagnostic verdict.\nrg_alpha = alpha_wide[\"AdamW + TraceLogRG\"].dropna()\nbase_alpha = alpha_wide[\"AdamW baseline\"].dropna()\nrg_below = rg_alpha.lt(2.0)\nbase_below = base_alpha.lt(2.0)\n\nfirst_rg_below = int(rg_below[rg_below].index[0]) if rg_below.any() else None\nfirst_base_below = int(base_below[base_below].index[0]) if base_below.any() else None\nfailures = int(summary[\"geometry failures\"])\nfired_fraction = float(summary[\"fraction actually corrected\"])\n\nif fired.empty:\n    projection_worked = False\nelse:\n    scale = float(fired[\"base_trace_log_drift\"].abs().mean())\n    tolerance = max(1e-8, 1e-3 * scale)\n    projection_worked = bool(np.isfinite(max_corrected) and max_corrected <= tolerance)\n\nprint(\"FC1 maximum-intervention diagnosis\")\nprint(\"-----------------------------------\")\nprint(\"Baseline first epoch below alpha=2:\", first_base_below)\nprint(\"TraceLogRG first epoch below alpha=2:\", first_rg_below)\nprint(f\"Every-step coverage fraction: {coverage:.6f}\")\nprint(f\"Fraction of FC1 steps corrected: {fired_fraction:.6f}\")\nprint(\"Geometry failures:\", failures)\nprint(\"Projection removed selected drift numerically:\", projection_worked)\nprint()\n\nif coverage < 0.99 or failures:\n    print(\n        \"VERDICT: invalid every-step test. Fix missing opportunities or geometry \"\n        \"failures before interpreting alpha.\"\n    )\nelif fired_fraction == 0.0:\n    print(\n        \"VERDICT: the one-sided trigger never fired. More correction strength \"\n        \"cannot help because there was no selected component to scale; the sign \"\n        \"criterion is not aligned with the observed alpha flow.\"\n    )\nelif not projection_worked:\n    print(\n        \"VERDICT: the maximum intervention did not numerically remove the selected \"\n        \"trace-log drift. Debug the projection implementation first.\"\n    )\nelif rg_below.any():\n    print(\n        \"VERDICT: the uncapped, full-strength, every-step one-sided projection \"\n        \"removed its selected trace-log drift, but FC1 still crossed below alpha=2. \"\n        \"The old 25-step cadence and 10% cap are not the explanation. The \"\n        \"trace-log-normal component alone is insufficient, or its one-sided sign \"\n        \"is not the alpha-controlling direction.\"\n    )\nelse:\n    print(\n        \"VERDICT: maximum every-step intervention prevented FC1 from crossing \"\n        \"below alpha=2. The original cadence and/or cap was too conservative.\"\n    )","outputs":[]},{"id":"1128e64a","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Scope\n\nThis notebook deliberately does **not** use $\\alpha$, $\\beta_E$, ERG gap, or correlation traps to alter the optimizer. It only tests the existing one-sided trace-log component removal at every step and without a cap.\n\nIf this maximum intervention removes the selected trace-log drift but FC1 still crosses below $\\alpha=2$, the next test should be the sign-independent `tangent` mode. A later, separate implementation can test an explicitly trace-log-preserving spectral-shape or $\\beta_E$ controller.","metadata":{}}]}